<title>CHINA: China's Yanjing becomes country's largest brewery.</title>
<headline>China's Yanjing becomes country's largest brewery.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Beijing Yanjing Brewery Co expanded to become China largest beer producer in 1996, the Beijing Economic Daily said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Its pre-tax profits were 357.99 million yuan ($43.13 million) in 1996, soaring by 58.2 percent compared with 1995. Total 1996 output of beer was 571,000 tonnes, 68.2 percent up from 1995, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>In 1996, Yanjing took 85 percent market share in Beijing and 25 percent in the nearby port city of Tianjin, it said. ($1 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>--Beijing Newsroom (8610) 65321921</p>
